      "traps": [
        "CRITICAL: direction of effect changes the drug. Gain-of-function variants (typically neonatal-onset seizures) showed 94% good-to-excellent phenytoin response; loss-of-function variants (typically autism/ID, later or no seizures) showed 0% (Brain, 2024).",
        "You CANNOT infer direction from the variant notation alone — it requires functional data. State that the distinction exists and is clinically decisive, and route it to genetics/neurology. Never guess a direction. Never imply a drug choice.",
